course: dictionary
lesson: 843
title: Beryl: a stone and a name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one the writer means. Beryl is one of these words. It can be a hard mineral that forms crystals, or it can be a girl's name.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Emeralds are green beryl, and the finest came from Colombia, where the Spanish took them from the 1500s.» Emeralds, colour, crystals and a place all tell you that beryl here is a stone, not a person.
explain: If a story says «Grandma Beryl baked a cake», then Beryl comes after Grandma and has a capital letter. That is a clue that it is a name. Always ask: is this word a thing, a person, or a place? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Beryl is a hard mineral that forms crystals.
fact: Beryl comes in many colours. Green beryl is emerald, and blue-green beryl is aquamarine.
fact: A mineral is a natural solid found in rocks and the ground.
fact: Beryl is also an old-fashioned girl's name, so it starts with a capital letter when it is a name.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word. Use it to decide which meaning fits.
exercise: «Emeralds are green beryl, and the finest came from Colombia.» What is green beryl called? | Ruby | *Emerald | Pearl
exercise: In a story, «Beryl gave her grandson a hug.» What is Beryl in this sentence? | A colour | *A name | A mineral
exercise: Aquamarine is a kind of beryl. What colour is it? | Black | Red | *Blue-green | Yellow
test: Beryl forms what kind of shape? | Puddles | Ropes | Clouds | *Crystals
test: In «Emeralds are green beryl, and the finest came from Colombia», where did the finest come from? | Spain | *Colombia | Scotland | Australia
exam: In science lessons, beryl is an example of what? | A kind of song | A bird | A planet | *A crystal mineral
